{
  "entries": [
    {
      "id": "j_will",
      "category": "EVENTS",
      "title": "The will",
      "text": "Stay in Vale Manor and find \"the Eighth Record\" before midnight on the seventh day. That is the whole condition. Nobody will say what the Eighth Record is.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "arrived"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_vale_manor",
      "category": "PLACES",
      "title": "Vale Manor",
      "text": "Outside Bellweather, Oregon. A stone wing from 1874, a great hall from 1911, a clapboard wing from 1926, a copper observatory, and the forest all round. Every generation added something. Nobody took anything away.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "arrived"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_family_vale",
      "category": "FAMILIES",
      "title": "The Vales",
      "text": "Either the Vales built Bellweather, or Bellweather was built around the Vales. The town can't seem to decide.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "arrived"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "u_eighth_record",
      "category": "UNRESOLVED",
      "title": "What is the Eighth Record?",
      "text": "A document? A book? A room? The will only names it.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "arrived"
      },
      "resolvedWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "ledger_read"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "u_why_me",
      "category": "UNRESOLVED",
      "title": "Why me?",
      "text": "I had never heard of Arthur Vale before the letter from his lawyers.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "arrived"
      },
      "resolvedWhen": {
        "type": "revelation",
        "id": "heir_is_orrin"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_arthur",
      "category": "PEOPLE",
      "title": "Arthur Vale",
      "text": "The last owner of Vale Manor. Died this September. He left me the house, on a condition, and a letter that opens with an apology for failing.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "document",
        "document": "doc_arthur_letter"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_executors",
      "category": "FAMILIES",
      "title": "Hawthorne & Mercer",
      "text": "Arthur's executors. Two old Bellweather names sharing one letterhead. \"We are not permitted to assist you further.\" Permitted by whom?",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "document",
        "document": "doc_executor_card"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "u_who_keeps_house",
      "category": "UNRESOLVED",
      "title": "Who keeps this house?",
      "text": "The front lock was freshly oiled. A lamp burns in the turret. Arthur was dying for months. Someone has been looking after the place — and paying for it.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "front_door_oiled"
      },
      "resolvedWhen": {
        "type": "revelation",
        "id": "who_paid"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_margaret",
      "category": "PEOPLE",
      "title": "Margaret Vale",
      "text": "1816–1891. Her portrait hangs in the entrance hall. She was painted with a pen in her hand, not a fan or a book. She wrote everything down.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "seen_portrait_margaret"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_elias",
      "category": "PEOPLE",
      "title": "Elias Vale",
      "text": "1812–1880. The first Vale here; came west in 1847. A surveyor. The portrait gives him a chain and dirty hands.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "seen_portrait_elias"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "u_ticking",
      "category": "UNRESOLVED",
      "title": "The ticking",
      "text": "The hall clock is stopped. Something to the west of the hall keeps time anyway.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "noticed_ticking"
      },
      "resolvedWhen": {
        "type": "puzzleSolved",
        "puzzle": "library_clock"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_study",
      "category": "PLACES",
      "title": "Arthur's study",
      "text": "The old drawing room, with the piano under a sheet. Boxes labelled with family names, all empty. A corkboard with nothing left on it but pinholes.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "visited:arthur_study"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_1936",
      "category": "EVENTS",
      "title": "The Bellweather Disappearance",
      "text": "17 November 1936. Eleven people at dinner in this house. By morning, none of them. Four were Vales.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "any",
        "of": [
          {
            "type": "document",
            "document": "doc_police_report_1936"
          },
          {
            "type": "document",
            "document": "doc_newspaper_1936"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "u_217",
      "category": "UNRESOLVED",
      "title": "Why 2:17?",
      "text": "The clock stopped at 2:17. Arthur wrote it down as if it were an instruction.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "any",
        "of": [
          {
            "type": "document",
            "document": "doc_police_report_1936"
          },
          {
            "type": "document",
            "document": "doc_arthur_note_217"
          }
        ]
      },
      "resolvedWhen": {
        "type": "puzzleSolved",
        "puzzle": "library_clock"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "u_measurements",
      "category": "UNRESOLVED",
      "title": "\"Room measurements don't match\"",
      "text": "A policeman's pencil, in 1936: the rooms don't fit inside the walls. Which rooms?",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "document",
        "document": "doc_police_report_1936"
      },
      "resolvedWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "passage_revealed"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_two_versions",
      "category": "DOCUMENTS",
      "title": "Two versions of one night",
      "text": "The police report: the west wing door was bolted from the inside, the clock stopped in the west library.\nThe newspaper: every door unlocked, the clock in the dining hall, a power failure.\nA power failure doesn't stop a wind-up clock.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "all",
        "of": [
          {
            "type": "document",
            "document": "doc_police_report_1936"
          },
          {
            "type": "document",
            "document": "doc_newspaper_1936"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_edmund",
      "category": "PEOPLE",
      "title": "Edmund Vale",
      "text": "Arthur's father. One of the eleven. Arthur was seven, at school in Portland.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "document",
        "document": "doc_newspaper_1936"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_seven_families",
      "category": "FAMILIES",
      "title": "The Meridian Society",
      "text": "October 1936, a month before the disappearance: seven chairs for seven families. One chair has been cut out of the print.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "document",
        "document": "doc_meridian_photo"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "u_refused",
      "category": "UNRESOLVED",
      "title": "\"One refused\"",
      "text": "\"Seven remained. One refused.\" Seven of what? Refused what?",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "read_photo_back"
      },
      "resolvedWhen": {
        "type": "document",
        "document": "doc_minutes_1871"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_julian",
      "category": "PEOPLE",
      "title": "Dr. Julian Whitmore",
      "text": "Arthur's pencil on the back of the photograph: \"Julian W.? — the eighth?\" Arthur also told me not to trust him.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "read_photo_back"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "u_julian",
      "category": "UNRESOLVED",
      "title": "Was Julian the eighth?",
      "text": "Arthur thought so for twenty years. Somebody cut Julian out of the photograph.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "read_photo_back"
      },
      "resolvedWhen": {
        "type": "revelation",
        "id": "julian_not_eighth"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "u_eight_marks",
      "category": "UNRESOLVED",
      "title": "Too many marks",
      "text": "In the photograph, the marks on the floor don't match the number of chairs.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "noticed_floor_marks"
      },
      "resolvedWhen": {
        "type": "revelation",
        "id": "photo_altered"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "u_knocking",
      "category": "UNRESOLVED",
      "title": "Knocking",
      "text": "Three knocks inside the study's west wall. I didn't answer.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "heard_knocking"
      },
      "resolvedWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "seen_counterweight"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_symbol_seven",
      "category": "SYMBOLS",
      "title": "Circle, line, seven points",
      "text": "Stamped on the brass study key. It looks like a seal. Whose?",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "hasItem",
        "item": "study_key"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_library",
      "category": "PLACES",
      "title": "The west library",
      "text": "Where the police found the clock stopped. The bulbs have been taken out of every fitting. A gallery runs round it, and an iron stair.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "visited:library"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_passage",
      "category": "PLACES",
      "title": "The seam",
      "text": "Between the 1911 hall and the 1874 wing, a gap a metre and a half wide that no plan shows. A door from the library behind a bookcase. A shaft with a counterweight in it. And the old wing's outer wall, still facing in.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "passage_revealed"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_symbol_eight",
      "category": "SYMBOLS",
      "title": "Circle, line, eight points",
      "text": "The same seal, with eight points. Cut into the old wing's stone before it was laid.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "seen_eight_point_symbol"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_releve",
      "category": "DOCUMENTS",
      "title": "Survey leaf, 1791",
      "text": "French, half a century before the Vales came. \"Huit points. Huit témoins.\" Eight points. Eight witnesses. And: the register was already there.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "read_releve"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_caretaker",
      "category": "PEOPLE",
      "title": "The caretaker",
      "text": "Comes on Mondays, paid by the Ashcroft Trust. Oils the locks, trims the turret lamp, never stays after dark, never opens the west wing. Standing instructions signed E.O., 1937.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "read_caretaker_book"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_west_wing",
      "category": "PLACES",
      "title": "The west wing",
      "text": "The stone house of 1874, sealed from the inside since 1936 and boarded up in 1938. The oldest rooms in the house, and the coldest.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "visited:west_wing"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_stone_1849",
      "category": "EVENTS",
      "title": "The stone, 1849",
      "text": "Two years after they came west, Elias dug a trial pit and hit dressed rock: a ring, a line running true north, eight points. Someone had set it there before any Vale.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "any",
        "of": [
          {
            "type": "flag",
            "key": "read_field_book"
          },
          {
            "type": "flag",
            "key": "read_margaret_diary"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_hannah",
      "category": "PEOPLE",
      "title": "Hannah Vale",
      "text": "1864–1940. Margaret's granddaughter. The one who meant to tell the truth.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "any",
        "of": [
          {
            "type": "flag",
            "key": "read_letter_1888"
          },
          {
            "type": "flag",
            "key": "read_observing_card"
          },
          {
            "type": "flag",
            "key": "read_hannah_note"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_found_it",
      "category": "EVENTS",
      "title": "\"He found it\"",
      "text": "Margaret, 1888: the Society was not founded by Elias. He found it — a circle, a line, eight points, already in the ground, already kept by someone. He filled seven chairs. The Orrins would not sit in the eighth.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "read_letter_1888"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "u_orrin",
      "category": "UNRESOLVED",
      "title": "The Orrins",
      "text": "A family that refused the eighth chair in 1871 — and whose name keeps turning up scraped off things.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "any",
        "of": [
          {
            "type": "flag",
            "key": "read_letter_1888"
          },
          {
            "type": "document",
            "document": "doc_minutes_1871"
          }
        ]
      },
      "resolvedWhen": {
        "type": "revelation",
        "id": "witness_erased"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_meridian",
      "category": "PLACES",
      "title": "The line",
      "text": "True north from the stone under the west wing: through the observatory, the sundial, a row of flagstones, and on into the trees to the family vault. Elias built everything on it.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "any",
        "of": [
          {
            "type": "flag",
            "key": "looked_down_the_line"
          },
          {
            "type": "flag",
            "key": "read_meridian_chart"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_observatory",
      "category": "PLACES",
      "title": "The observatory",
      "text": "1911, Hannah's. A copper dome on the line, with a telescope that, according to her, is not for stars.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "visited:observatory"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_nameless",
      "category": "SYMBOLS",
      "title": "The nameless stone",
      "text": "In the family plot: a stone with the name chiselled off. A year, 1871, and eight points.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "seen_nameless_stone"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_minutes",
      "category": "DOCUMENTS",
      "title": "The first sitting, 1871",
      "text": "Seven families and seven functions — Knowledge, Law, Industry, Medicine, Finance, Faith, Record — and an eighth: Witness, the eye. Offered to a J. Orr—, refused (\"We will not sit. We will only see.\"), and struck out. The Witness's book, kept apart.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "read_minutes_1871"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "u_witness_book",
      "category": "UNRESOLVED",
      "title": "The book kept apart",
      "text": "Margaret's diary, the 1871 minutes: the Witness's book is \"kept apart\". Where? And is it the Eighth Record?",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "any",
        "of": [
          {
            "type": "flag",
            "key": "read_margaret_diary"
          },
          {
            "type": "flag",
            "key": "read_minutes_1871"
          }
        ]
      },
      "resolvedWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "seen_witness_ledger"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_dinner",
      "category": "EVENTS",
      "title": "The dinner",
      "text": "The east wing table is still laid for the night of 17 November 1936: ten places with cards, and an eleventh at the foot, unused, with a card that says only W.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "any",
        "of": [
          {
            "type": "flag",
            "key": "read_place_cards"
          },
          {
            "type": "flag",
            "key": "seen_w_card"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_reckoning",
      "category": "EVENTS",
      "title": "The Reckoning",
      "text": "Once a generation the seven chairs went down by the seam and counted. In 1936 Edmund meant to have it witnessed, for the first time since 1871. At 2:17 the library clock struck and the counterweight shut the door behind them.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "read_order_of_night"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_eleanor",
      "category": "PEOPLE",
      "title": "Eleanor Orrin",
      "text": "Invited by Edmund to stand as Witness on 17 November 1936. Her train was held at Albany. She walked from the station.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "any",
        "of": [
          {
            "type": "flag",
            "key": "read_order_of_night"
          },
          {
            "type": "flag",
            "key": "read_telegram"
          },
          {
            "type": "flag",
            "key": "read_edmund_letter"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_pell",
      "category": "PEOPLE",
      "title": "Mrs. Ada Pell",
      "text": "The Vales' housekeeper; the eleventh of the eleven. She was told to stay above. She didn't burn the instructions.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "read_pell_daybook"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_ruth",
      "category": "PEOPLE",
      "title": "Ruth Orrin",
      "text": "Eleanor's daughter. Born 1946, died 1994. Left a sealed letter and a key at St. Brigid's, for a child she couldn't keep.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "any",
        "of": [
          {
            "type": "flag",
            "key": "read_st_brigid"
          },
          {
            "type": "flag",
            "key": "read_ruth_letter"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_rhyme",
      "category": "SYMBOLS",
      "title": "The counting rhyme",
      "text": "Eight lines, one word each. \"Count the points from the top and go the way the sun goes.\" The only key the Orrins were ever given.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "read_ruth_rhyme"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_payer",
      "category": "EVENTS",
      "title": "Who paid",
      "text": "From 1937 the Ashcroft Trust paid for the house, the boards, the roof, the lamp: authorised E.O. From 1971, A.V. as well. In 1968, one entry: \"rebinding, vellum, one volume\".",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "read_receipts"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_arthur_wrong",
      "category": "PEOPLE",
      "title": "What Arthur got wrong",
      "text": "Julian Whitmore was not the eighth — he sat as Medicine, and voted no. The house wasn't paid for by Hawthorne & Mercer, but by a woman who missed a train. And the book didn't hold the answer for him: it wasn't written for a Vale.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "all",
        "of": [
          {
            "type": "revelation",
            "id": "julian_not_eighth"
          },
          {
            "type": "any",
            "of": [
              {
                "type": "flag",
                "key": "read_eleanor_letter"
              },
              {
                "type": "flag",
                "key": "read_receipts"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_below",
      "category": "PLACES",
      "title": "Below the west wing",
      "text": "Under the old cellar, down Elias's well: a timbered tunnel of 1849 running north, a room with eight lamp niches, and a stone door older than the tunnel.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "visited:below"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_chamber",
      "category": "PLACES",
      "title": "The Meridian Chamber",
      "text": "A round stone room on the line. A brass circle in the floor, a gnomon, seven ledgers on seven lecterns, and an eighth book kept apart in a niche to the north.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "visited:meridian_chamber"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_eleven",
      "category": "EVENTS",
      "title": "Where they went",
      "text": "Down the seam, by a stair that ends at a stone door with no handle on the inside. Their things are still on the lowest steps.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "seen_1936_effects"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "j_eighth_record",
      "category": "DOCUMENTS",
      "title": "The Eighth Record",
      "text": "The Witness Ledger. The Orrins' book, written in the count. Kept apart, waiting for somebody who could read it.",
      "unlockWhen": {
        "type": "flag",
        "key": "ledger_read"
      }
    }
  ],
